<!-- 
| Feature/Gaps           | Status    | Technical Observation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **Register Map**       | **FULL**  | Populated strictly according to `i2c_reg.h`. Covers the unified configuration, interrupt, timing, and FIFO banks.                                                                                                                                                                     |
| **Base Address**       | Explicit  | 0x2000A300 (I2C0).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| **Unified Interrupt**  | **FULL**  | `i2c_int_sts` (0x04) is a complex unified register containing Status (bits 0-5), Masks (bits 8-13), Clear pulses (bits 16, 19, 20), and Enables (bits 24-29).                                                                                                                            |
| **Timing Phases**      | **FULL**  | Added high-resolution timing registers: `i2c_prd_start` (0x10), `i2c_prd_stop` (0x14), and `i2c_prd_data` (0x18). Each register defines 4 distinct phases (8-bits each) for SCL/SDA transitions.                                                                                         |
| **Sub-Addressing**     | **FULL**  | Integrated 4-byte hardware sub-addressing (`i2c_sub_addr` at 0x08), allowing the controller to automatically handle multi-byte register offsets.                                                                                                                                      |
| **FIFO Management**    | **FULL**  | `i2c_fifo_config_0` (0x80) includes hardware overflow/underflow flags and DMA triggers. `i2c_fifo_config_1` (0x84) provides 2-bit FIFO counters and 1-bit thresholding.                                                                                                                |
| **Reset Values**       | **FULL**  | Synchronized with header: `cr_i2c_pkt_dir` defaults to 1 (Read), `cr_i2c_scl_sync_en` defaults to 1 (Clock Stretching enabled). Timing phases default to 0xF.                                                                                                                          |
-->
